    <h1>Methodology and source library</h1>
    <p>Reports name the dataset, the date it was pulled, and the cleaning choices that change a number. Observed facts, derived metrics, and editorial indices are labeled separately so a reader can argue with the claim without guessing which kind of sentence it is.</p>
    <p>Charts and tables are built from public sources or from files the reader supplies. Each report lists those sources in its back matter. The grouped citation catalog is on the <a href="/sources">sources</a> page. Editorial standards are in the <a href="/legal/ethics-statement">ethics statement</a>.</p>
    <p>Exports (HTML, PDF, EPUB, CSV) are the record. If a figure and the prose disagree, the figure's source note wins until a correction is published.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
